# Optional: when running "npm start" on Mac against Pi backend instead of localhost.
# Create React App will NOT proxy; requests go directly to this URL.
# Omit to use the default "proxy" in package.json (localhost:3001).
#
# run-local.sh overrides this to http://localhost:3001/api/weather so the local
# backend (with NWS alerts, etc.) is used. If you "npm start" directly and have
# REACT_APP_API_URL set to the Pi, the app will hit the Pi (no NWS alerts there).
#
# Copy to .env.development.local and uncomment one line; or use: npm run start:pi
# REACT_APP_API_URL=http://towerhill.local:3001/api/weather
# REACT_APP_API_URL=http://192.168.1.160:3001/api/weather
#
# If you see "Tempest offline - showing cached data": from Mac run
#   curl -s http://towerhill.local:3001/health
# If that fails, try the Pi IP (e.g. http://192.168.1.160:3001/health). Use the IP in
# REACT_APP_API_URL if towerhill.local does not resolve on your Mac.
#
# If "npm start" fails with "allowedHosts[0] should be a non-empty string", add:
# DANGEROUSLY_DISABLE_HOST_CHECK=true